Write the minimal implementation. `toon_validation_error(e: &michi::toon::ToonError) -> michi::DomainError` builds a DomainError directly (not via ToDomainError, which is scoped only to MonoklError's closed 14-value set) with `ErrorCode::ExternalFailure` and `.retryable(false)`, for the case where this module's own row construction violates michi's own structural invariants -- a bug in this module, not a caller input error. `render_projection<const N, T: ToonProjection<N>>(value: &T) -> Result<String, michi::DomainError>` is the sole function converting a ToonProjection<N> into a rendered TOON string (AC-004B), verified step-by-step against michi's real pinned-rev source: builds a `ToonOptions` via `ToonOptions::new(T::TYPE_NAME, fields: Vec<String>, rows.clone())` (michi-toon/src/lib.rs's real signature takes `Vec<String>`, not `&[&str]`, so `T::FIELDS` is converted), calls `.total_count(value.toon_total_count())` (`ToonOptions::total_count` takes `Option<usize>` directly), then calls `.validate()` explicitly and returns `Err(toon_validation_error(&e))` on failure BEFORE ever constructing an `AgentResponse` -- this explicit call matters because `AgentResponse::toon_body()` DOES call `validate()` internally but on failure only affects body TEXT, never `is_error`/`isError` (verified directly: `crate::mcp::CallToolResult`'s `is_error` and `render_json`'s `"isError"` key both read only the builder's own `is_error` field, set exclusively via `AgentResponse::as_error()`, which `toon_body()`'s internal validate() failure never calls -- so an invalid ToonOptions handed straight to AgentResponse would render successfully-looking output). On success, builds `michi::AgentResponse::new(T::TYPE_NAME).items(rows, T::FIELDS.as_slice()).hints(value.toon_hints())` and returns `Ok(resp.render_toon())` -- `AgentResponse::render_toon()`, not the standalone `michi::toon::render_toon()` free function, since only the former's `finish_text()` appends `self.hints` (confirmed: `pub fn render_toon(&self) -> String { self.finish_text(&self.toon_body()) }`, crates/michi-core/src/response.rs), which is what makes AC-006's extract hint actually reach output. Also adds `projection_tests`: two end-to-end tests rendering a real SymbolsResult and SearchResponse through render_projection() and asserting on the exact rendered TOON text (proving AC-004/AC-005/AC-006/AC-004B together, not just that each compiles), an AC-014 test constructing a deliberately-mismatched ToonOptions by hand (the only way to trigger the failure path, since ToonProjection<N> itself makes a real mismatch impossible to construct) and asserting toon_validation_error's exact shape, and an AC-013 test proving `Value::Null` and `Value::from("")` render identically in a full TOON document. Run: `cat >> /Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/crates/monokl/src/output/agent.rs <<'RUSTEOF'
/// Constructs a `DomainError` directly from a `michi::toon::ToonError` --
/// deliberately not via `ToDomainError`, which is scoped only to
/// `MonoklError`'s closed `monokl_code()` set. Indicates a bug in this
/// module's own row/field construction, not a caller input error.
pub fn toon_validation_error(e: &michi::toon::ToonError) -> michi::DomainError {
    michi::DomainError::new(michi::ErrorCode::ExternalFailure, format!("toon_render_invalid: {e}")).retryable(false)
}

/// The sole function that converts a `ToonProjection<N>` implementation into
/// a rendered TOON string.
#[allow(clippy::result_large_err)] // AC-004B locks this exact signature verbatim against michi's own DomainError.
pub fn render_projection<const N: usize, T: ToonProjection<N>>(value: &T) -> Result<String, michi::DomainError> {
    let rows: Vec<Vec<Value>> = value.toon_rows().into_iter().map(|row| row.to_vec()).collect();
    let fields: Vec<String> = T::FIELDS.iter().map(|s| (*s).to_string()).collect();

    let opts = michi::toon::ToonOptions::new(T::TYPE_NAME, fields, rows.clone()).total_count(value.toon_total_count());
    if let Err(e) = opts.validate() {
        return Err(toon_validation_error(&e));
    }

    let mut resp = michi::AgentResponse::new(T::TYPE_NAME).items(rows, T::FIELDS.as_slice()).hints(value.toon_hints());
    if let Some(n) = value.toon_total_count() {
        resp = resp.total_count(n);
    }
    Ok(resp.render_toon())
}

